  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nHigh pressure remains spread across the eastern CONUS allowing for a \ncontinued period of dry weather. Slightly cooler today behind a dry \ncold front with highs in the mid to upper 60s. Southerly return flow \nwill allow for highs mid to late week to warm into the mid to upper \n70s, which is 10-15 degrees above average for late October. A few \nsites may approach record high values for October 29th. See the \nclimate section below for more information. \n\nAnother cold front will sink south towards the region Thursday night \nwhich may bring some rain showers to Northeast Ohio/Northwest \nPennsylvania. High pressure returns Friday into Saturday before rain \nchances approach from the west late Saturday into Sunday. Current \ntiming of this system would indicate a dry Halloween night for the \nmajority of the forecast area.",
